# Empty on purpose — every request is a relative path (e.g. /api/events),
# resolved against whatever origin the page is actually loaded from. In
# production, Amplify's rewrite rule (Console → Rewrites and redirects)
# transparently proxies /api/* to the Railway backend, so the browser never
# sees a cross-origin request at all — required for document.cookie reads
# (session.js) to work, since that's strictly same-origin no matter what
# cookie attributes are set. Local dev gets the same behavior via
# vite.config.js's dev-server proxy.
VITE_API_URL=https://acceptable-commitment-production-d2e1.up.railway.app
VITE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=15000